hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24161","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Sa'd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi narrated to me, from Qays ibn Amr, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw a man praying two rakahs after the morning prayer, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The morning prayer twice? The man said: I had not prayed the two rakahs before them, so I prayed them now. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was silent."
"24162","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I heard Abd Rabbih ibn Said, brother of Yahya ibn Said, narrating from his grandfather, he said: He went out to morning and found the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the morning, and he had not bowed the two rakahs of dawn. He prayed with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then stood when he finished the morning and bowed the two rakahs of dawn. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by him and said: What is this prayer? He told him, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was silent and went on, and said nothing."
